## My manual

#### Why I keep this

[[What I hope this journal does for me.]]

To notice how I'm actually doing before it turns into a bad week. Two minutes a day, not a project.
I want to look back at a month and see a pattern, not a pile of guilt.

#### What I do

[[Written from my template. After each one, why it is there; cross out what I don’t use.]]

Each week begins:

- This week (3 task lines) — three things, never more. If a fourth shows up, one comes off.

Each day:

- Energy (a scale, 1–5, empty to full) — the first thing I fill in, before coffee. A guess is fine.
- Care (boxes: Meds, Water, Outside) — the basics. A ticked box is a win, not a minimum.
- Today (room to write) — one line is enough. More only if I want to.

Each week ends:

- What went well (room to write) — first, always, even if it's small.
- What to change (room to write) — one thing to try next week, not a list of faults.

#### My marks

[[What each mark means to me, and when I use it.]]

- `[ ]` a task — only things I mean to do this week.
- `[x]` done — 
- `[>]` moved to another day — moved once is fine; moved twice means it gets a decision.
- `[<]` scheduled for later — I don't use this one.
- `[-]` not doing it after all — a decision, not a failure. I cross it off on purpose.
- `[!]` important — at most one a day.
- `o` an event — appointments, and anything with a time.
- `?` a question to come back to — I read these on Sunday.
- `!` an idea — stays here until it has a next step.

#### What I skip on purpose

[[What I leave out, so leaving it out is a choice and not a failure.]]

No colours, no stickers, no drawing the layout. No word counts, no streaks.
Weekends are optional: if I skip Saturday and Sunday, the week still counts.

#### After a gap

[[How I start again after days away, without catching up.]]

Start with today's date. Don't fill in the missed days. If something from the gap matters, one line under today: "Last week: …".

#### When I revise this

[[When I read this manual again and change it: the start of each month, say.]]

The first of each month, before I download the new month. If the template changes, this changes with it.
Last revised: 2026-11-01.

